  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_scope",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": -300,
        "y": 120
      },
      "text": "REAR FUEL - fuel level sender behind IX_FUEL_LVL (DT04-2P on the ECU/cabin harness, DT06-2S here), plus the fuel pump run. Rev 2 (Dan, 2026-10-10): the sender gets a DT 2-way instead of its OEM connector - DT04-2P + W2P on the sender lead, size-16 contacts 0460-202-1631 (owned); no OEM housing. Everything in the trunk (IX_FUEL_LVL, sender, pump, ground stud) also moved to the driver side - see docs/HARNESS-CONSOLIDATION-AND-LAYOUT-PLAN.md / Route 11. FUEL PUMP (DECISIONS R75, 2026-10-14): the pump feed starts at the fuel pump relay k_fp (HCR150 terminal 5) in the battery relay block, trunk passenger side (ST185-HeavyDC, broken off) and runs unbroken, 10 AWG, across the trunk to the pump's own connector - no extra joint in the pump circuit (plan 6.41); 12 AWG return to the trunk ground stud. Run lengths are estimates - measure at install."
    }
  ],
